<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes:1.The financial results have been reviewed &amp; recommended by Audit Committee &amp; approved by Board of Directors at the meeting held on 4.2.23.2.The consolidated financial results have been prepared in accordance with recognition &amp; measurement principles laid down under Indian Accounting Standard(Ind AS)as prescribed under Sec 133 of the Companies Act,2013 read with relevant rules issued thereunder &amp; other accounting principles generally accepted in India in terms of Reg. 33 of SEBI (Listing Obligations &amp; Disclosure Requirements) Regulations,2015.3.Group is mainly engaged in business of manufacturing of Specialty Chemicals for Textile,Home &amp; Personal Care,Performance Chemicals &amp; Animal Health &amp; Nutrition industries.There are no reportable segments in accordance with IND AS 108–Operating Segments.4.During quarter ended 31.12.22,Parent Company has allotted 19,250 equity shares of Rs. 2.00 each pursuant to exercise of options under the approved Rossari Employee Stock Option Plan(ESOP)-2019.Subsequent to quarter end, on 19.01.23,Parent Co. has alloted 3,600 equity shares of Rs. 2.00 each pursuant to exercise of options under the approved Rossari ESOP-2019.5.From 01.04.22,Group has changed method of inventory valuation from First In First Out (FIFO) to Weighted Average Computation (WAC) which is most prevalent method followed in Specialty Chemicals industry.The impact due to aforesaid change is not significant to the financial results for current &amp; previous period.Accounting impact of the same has been applied prospectively.6.Parent had completed acquisition of Unitop Chemicals Private Limited (UCPL)&amp;Tristar Intermediates Private Limited (TIPL) on 26.08.21 and 30.08.21 respectively &amp; accounted for aforesaid acqusitions in its books as business acquisition in terms of Ind AS-103- 'Business Combination'.The results for current 9 months &amp; 9 months ended 31.12.21(corresponding 9 months) are not comparable.7.During the quarter ended 31.12.21,Parent Co. had completed the process of the acquisition/subscription of equity shares of 50.10% of issued and paid-up share capital of Romakk Chemicals Private Limited (Romakk),an associate of the Company,at an aggregate consideration of Rs.75.10 million.As per IND AS 103, allocation of purchase consideration towards the fair value of assets &amp; liabilities &amp; determination of goodwill were done on a provisional basis,pending final determination.During current quarter,Parent Co. has finalised fair valuation of assets &amp; liabilties which had been accounted on provisional basis in the quarter ended 31.12.21.The determination of such fair value has been carried out by independent agency appointed by Parent Company.The financial effect of revision is not material.   For ROSSARI BIOTECH LIMITED   EDWARD MENEZES   Executive Chairman    DIN:00149205   Place : Mumbai   Date:04.02.23</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
